{
  "sn6.4:0.1": "Linked Discourses 6.4 ",
  "sn6.4:0.2": "1. The Appeal ",
  "sn6.4:0.3": "With Baka the Divinity ",
  "sn6.4:1.1": "So I have heard. ",
  "sn6.4:1.2": "At one time the Buddha was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. ",
  "sn6.4:1.3": "Now at that time Baka the Divinity had the following harmful misconception: ",
  "sn6.4:1.4": "“This is permanent, this is everlasting, this is eternal, this is whole, this is not liable to pass away. For this is where there’s no being born, growing old, dying, passing away, or being reborn. And there’s no other escape beyond this.” ",
  "sn6.4:2.1": "Then the Buddha knew Baka the Divinity’s train of thought. As easily as a strong person would extend or contract their arm, he vanished from Jeta’s Grove and reappeared in that realm of divinity. ",
  "sn6.4:2.2": "Baka the Divinity saw the Buddha coming off in the distance ",
  "sn6.4:2.3": "and said to him, ",
  "sn6.4:2.4": "“Come, good fellow! Welcome, good fellow! ",
  "sn6.4:2.5": "It’s been a long time since you took the opportunity to come here. ",
  "sn6.4:2.6": "For this is permanent, this is everlasting, this is eternal, this is whole, this is not liable to pass away. For this is where there’s no being born, growing old, dying, passing away, or being reborn. And there’s no other escape beyond this.” ",
  "sn6.4:3.1": "When he had spoken, the Buddha said to him, ",
  "sn6.4:3.2": "“Alas, Baka the Divinity is lost in ignorance! Alas, Baka the D